@startuml
title CNC Motion Control — System Overview (scurve_motion, March 2026)
' Architecture: inline G-code dispatch, S-curve trajectory planner (64-slot),
' DDS interpolator, single TIMER_4_ISR (Bresenham + velocity, IPL6 shadow regs).
' No gcode command queue for normal streaming — motion_bridge.c receives events
' directly from gcode_parser.c. Arc segments generated in motion_bridge.c.
!theme blueprint

participant "UART3\nRing Buffer\n(1024 B RX/TX)" as UART
participant "gcode_parser.c\n(GCODE_Tasks\nInline Dispatch)" as PARSER
participant "motion_bridge.c\n(Event Handler\nArc State Machine)" as BRIDGE
participant "trajectory.c\n(S-curve Planner\n64-slot Ring)" as TRAJ
participant "kinematics.c\n(Work↔Machine\nCoord Transform)" as KIN
participant "interpolator.c\n(DDS Generator\n100 kHz tick)" as INTERP
participant "TIMER_4_ISR\n(IPL6 Shadow Regs\nBresenham + Velocity)" as ISR
participant "TMR5\n(One-Shot\n~2.56 µs pulse)" as TMR5
participant "Step GPIO\n(Harmony Macros)" as GPIO

== G-code Reception ==
UART -> PARSER : UART3 ring buffer → rxBuffer[] (UART3_ISR fills ring)
PARSER -> PARSER : service_realtime_byte() scanned first on every byte:\n  '?'  → build + send status string, no "ok"\n  '!'  → set g_feed_hold_active, no "ok"\n  '~'  → clear feed hold, no "ok"\n  Ctrl+X → PARSER_SoftReset(), send Grbl banner\n  0x90–0x9D → feed/rapid/spindle overrides, no "ok"\n  0x85 → jog cancel\n  G-code bytes preserved in push-back slot during realtime scan
PARSER -> PARSER : Accumulate until \\n or \\r terminator
PARSER -> PARSER : Strip comments, strip whitespace, uppercase

== System Commands ($H, $$, $n=v …) ==
PARSER -> PARSER : Route $-prefix lines to system command handler
PARSER -> BRIDGE : HOME event {axes_mask from $22}\n  (via inline dispatch — same path as G-code)
PARSER -> UART : "ok\\r\\n" or "error:N\\r\\n"

== Linear / Rapid Move (G0 / G1) ==
PARSER -> BRIDGE : LINEAR_MOVE event inline\n  {x,y,z,a, feedrate, is_rapid}
BRIDGE -> KIN : KINEMATICS_WorkToMachine(pos, modal_state)\n  Applies: active WCS (G54–G59) + G92 + TLO (G43/G43.1)
KIN -> BRIDGE : Machine-space CoordinatePoint
BRIDGE -> TRAJ : TRAJECTORY_AddMove(start_mach, end_mach, feedrate)
TRAJ -> TRAJ : normalise unit_vec[]\n  limit_acceleration_by_axis()\n  limit_rate_by_axis()\n  Junction: cos_theta = -dot(prev_unit, curr_unit)\n            sin_half  = sqrt(0.5*(1-cos_theta))\n            v²_junc   = accel × jdev × sin_half / (1-sin_half)
TRAJ -> TRAJ : Enqueue MotionSegment → MOTION_PlannerRecalculate():\n  1. Reverse pass  — cap entry by next-segment decel constraint\n  2. Forward pass  — cap entry by preceding-segment accel constraint\n  3. Trapezoid pass — write initial/nominal/final_rate,\n                      accelerate_until, decelerate_after
PARSER -> PARSER : Flow control — defer "ok" if traj queue ≥ HIGH_WATER (48)

== Arc Move (G2 / G3) ==
PARSER -> BRIDGE : ARC_MOVE event inline\n  {end, I/J/K, feedrate, is_CW, plane}
BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : Validate: |r_start−r_end| < $13 → ALARM:5 on fail
BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : armArcState = ARC_ACTIVE\n  Store: centre, radius, theta, thetaEnd, increment, arcEnd
loop One chord per APP_Tasks() iteration — non-blocking
  BRIDGE -> KIN : arc point (cx+r·cos θ, cy+r·sin θ) → machine coords
  KIN -> BRIDGE : machine-space point
  BRIDGE -> TRAJ : TRAJECTORY_AddMove(arcCurrent, next, feedrate)
  TRAJ -> TRAJ : Enqueue + MOTION_PlannerRecalculate()
  BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : theta += increment; arcCurrent = next
  alt Trajectory queue full (backpressure)
    BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : service_realtime_byte() — answer '?' queries
    note right of BRIDGE
      UGS status queries answered during backpressure.
      G-code bytes protected by push-back slot.
      No UGS timeout during long arcs.
    end note
  end
end
note right of BRIDGE
  Last segment uses exact arcEnd target — no accumulated
  floating-point error at arc termination.
end note

== Interpolator — Segment Load (main loop, every APP_Tasks) ==
INTERP -> INTERP : trajectory ring non-empty + no currentSegment?\n  → Load next MotionSegment into ISR statics:\n    delta[], abs_delta[], direction_bits, error[],\n    initial_rate, accelerate_until, decelerate_after
INTERP -> GPIO : DirX/Y/Z/A_Set/Clear — direction stable BEFORE first STEP
INTERP -> ISR : TMR4_Start() if not running — motion begins

== Per-Step Cycle (TIMER_4_InterruptHandler — IPL6) ==
ISR -> GPIO : OC1 dual-compare hardware auto-toggles dominant-axis STEP HIGH\n  (silicon — zero CPU cost for rising edge)
activate ISR
note over ISR
  M14K Shadow Register Set (IPL6):
  Entire CPU register file swapped in hardware in 1 cycle.
  Zero push/pop stack cost on ISR entry/exit.
end note
ISR -> ISR : Guard: seg = currentSegment; return if NULL
ISR -> GPIO : switch(dominant_axis) → Harmony macro → single LATxSET write\n  (compiler emits jump table — no function call, no pointer indirection)
ISR -> ISR : AXIS_IncrementSteps / AXIS_DecrementSteps (always_inline)
loop Bresenham subordinate axes (0–3, bounded worst-case)
  ISR -> ISR : error[axis] += abs_delta[axis]
  alt error[axis] >= dominant_delta
    ISR -> GPIO : switch(axis) → StepY/Z/A_Set() → single LATxSET
    ISR -> ISR : position counter; error[axis] -= dominant_delta
  end
end
ISR -> TMR5 : T5CONSET direct SFR — start one-shot pulse-width timer
ISR -> ISR : Velocity profile (integer only — no float, no division):\n  sc < accelerate_until  → step_interval -= rate_delta\n  sc >= decelerate_after → step_interval += decel_rate_delta\n  cruise                 → unchanged
ISR -> ISR : PR4 = step_interval (direct SFR, min clamp 7 ticks)
ISR -> ISR : seg->steps_completed++\n  if complete: T4CONCLR inside ISR; motionSegmentCompleted = true
deactivate ISR
TMR5 -> GPIO : ~2.56 µs: StepX/Y/Z/A_Clear() — 4 unrolled Harmony macros\n  All axes cleared unconditionally. DRV8825 min: 1 µs; TMC5160 min: 100 ns.

== Segment Completion (main loop — interpolator.c) ==
INTERP -> INTERP : steps_completed >= steps_remaining?\n  → currentSegment = NULL\n  → motionSegmentCompleted = true (triggers deferred "ok" check)\n  → Load next segment if queue non-empty\n  → TMR4_Stop() if queue empty; motionActive = false

== Safety ==
note over PARSER, GPIO
  g_feed_hold_active       — set by '!';  cleared by '~' or soft reset
  g_feed_hold_pending      — set by '!';  cleared when queue drains to 0
  g_suppress_hard_limits   — set by Ctrl+X; cleared when limits physically release
  g_estop_pending          — INT3 (RF4) IPL7 → STEPPER_DisableAll() + APP_ALARM
  INT1 (RF3) IPL6          — probe contact; latch probePosition, stop interpolator
  Hard limit check         — MOTION_UTILS_CheckHardLimits() every APP_Tasks
end note

@enduml